  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation (RBC-TOC-02) for 5 St. Brigid patients:\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005): Furosemide changed to 40 mg BID per signed addendum doc-00009 (mr-t0001). KCl stopped. Omeprazole kept (pantoprazole was a formulary substitution, not ordered). Lisinopril first kept on hold (K 5.4 on 10/21). A repeat BMP arrived 10/23 (K 4.7, SCr 1.21), so lisinopril was resumed (mr-00072). Earlier task-t0003 is now moot; I messaged you because I couldn't close it. Unsigned draft addendum proposing furosemide 60 mg BID (doc-00902) not acted on. Notes doc-t0004, doc-t0019.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004): First raised carvedilol to 12.5 BID per summary. A signed addendum arrived (doc-00904; bradycardia) reversing it, so carvedilol is back at 6.25 mg BID (mr-t0016). FLAGGED TO YOU: atorvastatin 80 mg fill coverage about 24% (§5b, unchanged, comm-t0006); outside glipizide 5 mg from Dr. Desai not addressed by discharge (§5a, not ordered, comm-t0007). Notes doc-t0008, doc-t0020.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044): Lisinopril resumed on SCr 1.08 and K 4.6 (10/22). Then K 5.5 on 10/23 (obs-09002) arrived, so lisinopril was re-held per §7. Task-t0018 for you, due 10/27. Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged. Notes doc-t0010, doc-t0021.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069): Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (post-discharge SCr 1.12, K 4.4 on 10/21). Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. Note doc-t0012 (one med-reference line in it is garbled: amlodipine is mr-69002, atorvastatin mr-69001).\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067): Metformin ER stays held. The only SCr (1.21) is from the hospital stay, not post-discharge. Task-t0013 for you, due 10/24 when the post-discharge BMP is expected. Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged. Note doc-t0014.\n\nAll fill adherence was 80% or above except Stark's atorvastatin. The 4 arrival inbox items were reviewed and closed.",
